--TEST--
`current()` outside the iteration protocol throws `LogicError`, at both of the points ADR 0053 § 1 names, and a `foreach` never reaches either
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Counting {
    // ADR 0053 § 4 lowers this to a state machine whose `current` reads the
    // parked element; § 1 is what says the read is guarded.
    public static function upTo(int $n): Iterator<int> {
        int $i = 1;
        while ($i <= $n) {
            yield $i;
            $i = $i + 1;
        }
    }
}

var $it = Counting::upTo(2);

// ADR 0053 § 1: before the first `advance()`. The slot holds the element type's
// null payload here, so an unguarded read would answer `0` rather than throw.
try {
    echo $it->current(), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "before: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// The protocol itself — the one place `current()` answers.
while ($it->advance()) {
    echo "in: ", $it->current(), "\n";
}

// ADR 0053 § 1: after `advance()` returned false. The slot still holds the last
// element, so an unguarded read would answer `2` — the more misleading half of
// the two, since it looks like an answer.
try {
    echo $it->current(), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "after: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// The guard sits on the accepted side for every iteration a `foreach` drives:
// it advances and reads in lockstep, so it never stands outside the protocol.
foreach (Counting::upTo(3) as int $v) {
    echo "each: ", $v, "\n";
}

// A generator whose body yields nothing is exhausted by its first `advance()`,
// so both of § 1's points are the same point for it.
try {
    var $empty = Counting::upTo(0);
    echo "advance: ", $empty->advance() ? "true" : "false", "\n";
    echo $empty->current(), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "empty: ", $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
before: current() outside the iteration protocol: it answers only after advance() returned true
in: 1
in: 2
after: current() outside the iteration protocol: it answers only after advance() returned true
each: 1
each: 2
each: 3
advance: false
empty: current() outside the iteration protocol: it answers only after advance() returned true
